BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Cavalaire-sur-Mer//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Cavalaire-sur-Mer — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Soupe de poissons de roche — Rockfish simmered and sieved into a rust-coloured broth\, with rouille and croutons.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soop de pwa-SON de rosh. What the coast actually eats when it is not eating bouillabaisse. Best: Maurin des Maures\, Le Rayol-Canadel — on the corniche\, open year-round per its listings\; call
LOCATION:Maurin des Maures\, Le Rayol-Canadel — on the corniche\, open year-round per its listings\; call
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Maurin+des+Maures+Rayol-Canadel+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bouillabaisse — Several rockfish cooked one after another in a saffron broth\; the broth first\, the fish after.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-ya-BESS. Marseille’s dish\, but this bay orders it the day before\, for at least two people. Best: Maurin des Maures\, Le Rayol-Canadel — order it the day before
LOCATION:Maurin des Maures\, Le Rayol-Canadel — order it the day before
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Maurin+des+Maures+Rayol-Canadel+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:The morning catch — Rascasse\, girelle and chapon for soup\, bream and bass\, sometimes a spider crab.
DESCRIPTION:Say: lah PESH doo ZHOOR. Bought off the boat on the quay\, the way the port has always sold it. Best: The fishermen’s stand\, Quai Marc Pajot — mid-morning\, weather and catch permitting
LOCATION:The fishermen’s stand\, Quai Marc Pajot — mid-morning\, weather and catch permitting
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Quai+Marc+Pajot+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Grand aïoli — Garlic emulsion with salt cod\, boiled vegetables\, snails and egg.
DESCRIPTION:Say: grahn eye-OH-lee. Provence stops for it\; eat it once\, slowly. Best: Le Comptoir des Saveurs\, Nouveau Port — seasonal\; check it is open
LOCATION:Le Comptoir des Saveurs\, Nouveau Port — seasonal\; check it is open
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Comptoir+des+Saveurs+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tapenade and anchoïade — Olive-and-caper paste\, and anchovy-and-garlic paste\, on bread with the first glass.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ta-pe-NAD · an-sho-YAD. The two smears of the apéro\; the name tapenade comes from the Provençal for the caper. Best: The Wednesday market\, Place Jean Moulin — mornings\, year-round
LOCATION:The Wednesday market\, Place Jean Moulin — mornings\, year-round
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+Jean+Moulin+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panisses — Fried batons of set chickpea flour\, eaten with salt.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-NEESS. Marseille street food with Ligurian roots\, sold on this coast too. Best: The Wednesday market\, Place Jean Moulin — if a stall fries them that morning
LOCATION:The Wednesday market\, Place Jean Moulin — if a stall fries them that morning
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+Jean+Moulin+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Daube provençale — Beef braised for hours in red wine with orange peel and olives.
DESCRIPTION:Say: dohb pro-vahn-SAL. The winter dish of the hills\; on the port it comes as beef cheek. Best: Le Comptoir des Saveurs\, Nouveau Port — the daube of beef cheek\; seasonal
LOCATION:Le Comptoir des Saveurs\, Nouveau Port — the daube of beef cheek\; seasonal
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Comptoir+des+Saveurs+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tarte tropézienne — A sugar-crusted brioche filled with two creams.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tart tro-pay-ZYEN. Named\, the story goes\, at Bardot’s suggestion on a film set in 1955. Best: La Tarte Tropézienne\, the house Alexandre Micka founded\, Saint-Tropez
LOCATION:La Tarte Tropézienne\, the house Alexandre Micka founded\, Saint-Tropez
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Tarte+Tropezienne+Saint-Tropez+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Marrons glacés — Whole chestnuts candied slowly in syrup\; and the crème de marrons\, the jar you carry home.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ma-RON gla-SAY. The Maures’ single-kernel chestnut\, turned into sugar in the village that grows it. Best: The confectioners of Collobrières\, forty minutes inland
LOCATION:The confectioners of Collobrières\, forty minutes inland
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Collobrieres+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Côtes de Provence rosé — Pale\, dry pink from Grenache\, Cinsault and friends\, drunk young and cold.
DESCRIPTION:Say: koht de pro-VAHNS ro-ZAY. Nine bottles in ten of the appellation are pink\; buy it at the estate\, not the beach club. Best: Domaine de la Croix\, La Croix-Valmer — at the cellar
LOCATION:Domaine de la Croix\, La Croix-Valmer — at the cellar
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+de+la+Croix+La+Croix-Valmer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cru Classé rosé — A rosé from one of the estates ranked in 1955.
DESCRIPTION:Say: krew kla-SAY. A classified growth you can drink in sight of the vines that made it. Best: Château Minuty\, Gassin — at the cellar door
LOCATION:Château Minuty\, Gassin — at the cellar door
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chateau+Minuty+Gassin+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tibouren — The peninsula’s old red grape\, made into a savoury\, garrigue-scented rosé.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tee-boo-REN. The one Provence pink that tastes of this coast rather than of fashion. Best: Ask for it at the estates of the peninsula\; La Grange à Vins\, La Croix-Valmer\, can pour one
LOCATION:Ask for it at the estates of the peninsula\; La Grange à Vins\, La Croix-Valmer\, can pour one
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Grange+a+Vins+La+Croix-Valmer+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rolle — Vermentino by its local name: a white of citrus pith and salt.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ROLL. The partner the morning catch actually wants. Best: Domaine La Tourraque\, Ramatuelle — inside the protected capes
LOCATION:Domaine La Tourraque\, Ramatuelle — inside the protected capes
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+La+Tourraque+Ramatuelle+Var+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:cavalaire-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pastis — Anise spirit with five parts cold water\, poured before lunch in the shade.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pas-TEESS. Marseille’s drink\, and the hour the whole coast keeps. Best: Any port café\; Ô Petit Bar on the marina for the hour
LOCATION:Any port café\; Ô Petit Bar on the marina for the hour
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=O+Petit+Bar+Cavalaire-sur-Mer+Var+France
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
